            "body": {
                "serial": "container_containerstatic_65018d7009a6e758184578",
                "body": "\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\"><em>Some</em><strong>text</strong>, yes, </div>\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\">then table</div>\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\">\n      {{table_65018d7009aed081494088}}\n      <p>then stimulus</p>\n      <p> </p>\n      <div class=\"tao-xjl5dyodm\">\n    \n        <div class=\"grid-row\"><div class=\"col-12\"><div class=\"colrow\"><p>\n{{img_65018d7009bc9676081630}}\n\n\n\n <span> </span></p></div></div></div><div class=\"grid-row\"><div class=\"col-12\"><div class=\"custom-text-box tao-a15ppo59w\">\n<p>Recent evidence suggests that the more time young people spend on social media, the more likely they are to be depressed. Researchers from the University of Pittsburgh asked 1,787 Americans aged between 19 and 32 to track the time they spent on social media. Participants were also assessed for depression using a questionnaire. The results showed that participants who used social media very frequently were more than twice as likely to be depressed as those who used it less often.</p>\n</div></div></div>\n    \n</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\"> then image {{img_65018d7009be2280003150}} then media</div>\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\">\n      {{qtiobject_65018d7009b9e935104115}}\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"x-tao-wrapper x-tao-relatedOutcome-RESPONSE\"> </div>\n  ",
                "elements": {
